r family in bergamo  even if the pandemic has made physical  distances more painful  in my heart my beloved worlds are even  closer  some envisioned a better world like a  miami resident who thinks more public  transit could reconnect the city once  lockdowns lift  access to nature seemed to make all the  difference in sydney australia  a reader found herself looking closer at  the trees on her block  in the uk a writer sketched what she  called a beautiful old canyon near our  house  that looks like a lost world though each  submission was unique  put together these maps show how the  emotional experiences of the coronavirus  pandemic  have been shared by people all around  the world  as economies reopen and a wave of  protests  fill formerly empty streets public and  private spaces are shifting once again  as society struggle to balance the  sweeping impacts of the pandemic  and a massive call to address systemic  racism and injustice  as a powerful medium for revealing our  relationships to place  these maps serve as a reminder of the  ways we are still connected  especially through times of upheaval and  as new futures  are forged  you
 

